$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 12/Effect and precision

::EPI-W12-022::What does a wide confidence interval usually indicate? {
=Low precision and compatibility with a wider range of effect sizes#Correct.
~No bias by definition#Review the appraisal question before choosing an interpretation.
~No effect by definition#Review the appraisal question before choosing an interpretation.
~Perfect generalisability#Review the appraisal question before choosing an interpretation.
}

::EPI-W12-023::Outcome risk is 5% in the exposed/intervention group and 8% in comparison. What is the risk ratio approximately? {
=0.62#Correct. Divide the two risks.
~1.60#Relative effect is a ratio, not an absolute difference.
~3.00#Relative effect is a ratio, not an absolute difference.
~0.38#Relative effect is a ratio, not an absolute difference.
}

::EPI-W12-024::Outcome risk is 5% versus 8%. What is the absolute risk difference, intervention minus comparison? {
=-3 percentage points#Correct. Risk difference subtracts the comparison risk from intervention/exposure risk.
~0.62 percentage points#Keep the direction of subtraction explicit.
~3 percentage points#Keep the direction of subtraction explicit.
~13 percentage points#Keep the direction of subtraction explicit.
}

