$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 12/P values

::EPI-W12-041::What does a small p-value NOT tell you? {
=That bias and confounding are absent#Correct.
~That the observed data are less compatible with a specified null model#Review the appraisal question before choosing an interpretation.
~That a statistical test was performed#Review the appraisal question before choosing an interpretation.
~That sample size can influence inference#Review the appraisal question before choosing an interpretation.
}

::EPI-W12-042::A study reports p\=0.08 with a wide confidence interval spanning meaningful benefit and harm. Which conclusion is best? {
=The study is imprecise and does not establish absence of an important effect#Correct.
~There is definitively no effect#Non-significance is not proof of no meaningful effect.
~The null hypothesis has an 8% probability of being true#Non-significance is not proof of no meaningful effect.
~Bias is impossible#Non-significance is not proof of no meaningful effect.
}

::EPI-W12-043::When appraising a cohort paper, a study reports p\=0.08 with a wide confidence interval spanning meaningful benefit and harm. Which conclusion is best? {
=The study is imprecise and does not establish absence of an important effect#Correct.
~There is definitively no effect#Non-significance is not proof of no meaningful effect.
~The null hypothesis has an 8% probability of being true#Non-significance is not proof of no meaningful effect.
~Bias is impossible#Non-significance is not proof of no meaningful effect.
}

$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 12/Applicability

::EPI-W12-044::What is internal validity primarily concerned with? {
=Credibility of the estimate for the study population under the design#Correct.
~Whether every country will have the same effect#Review the appraisal question before choosing an interpretation.
~Whether the result has a small p-value#Review the appraisal question before choosing an interpretation.
~Whether participants liked the intervention#Review the appraisal question before choosing an interpretation.
}

::EPI-W12-045::A highly internally valid trial was conducted in a specialised urban hospital. What must be considered before applying it to rural primary care? {
=Differences in population, implementation conditions and causal mechanisms#Correct.
~Only whether p is below 0.05#Applicability requires a context argument.
~Nothing; internal validity guarantees universal transport#Applicability requires a context argument.
~Only the font used in the report#Applicability requires a context argument.
}

::EPI-W12-046::When reviewing a cross-sectional report, a highly internally valid trial was conducted in a specialised urban hospital. What must be considered before applying it to rural primary care? {
=Differences in population, implementation conditions and causal mechanisms#Correct.
~Only whether p is below 0.05#Applicability requires a context argument.
~Nothing; internal validity guarantees universal transport#Applicability requires a context argument.
~Only the font used in the report#Applicability requires a context argument.
}

::EPI-W12-047::When reading a case-control study, a highly internally valid trial was conducted in a specialised urban hospital. What must be considered before applying it to rural primary care? {
=Differences in population, implementation conditions and causal mechanisms#Correct.
~Only whether p is below 0.05#Applicability requires a context argument.
~Nothing; internal validity guarantees universal transport#Applicability requires a context argument.
~Only the font used in the report#Applicability requires a context argument.
}

